    "https://jobs.purchase.edu/postings/1776": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Purchase College Portal | Assistant Professor of Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F069P Job Title Assistant Professor of Psychology Application Deadline 01/09/2027 Department School of Natural and Social Sciences FT - PT Full Time Part-time % Minimum Salary 65000.00 Maximum Salary 65000.00 Description The Department of Psychology at SUNY Purchase invites applications for an open-area tenure-track Assistant Professor of Psychology position beginning Fall 2027. SUNY Purchase is a primarily undergraduate, Hispanic-serving institution located 25 miles north of New York City, renowned for its conservatory programs in visual and performing arts. Purchase is ranked by US News in the Top 10 public US liberal arts colleges and is among the Best 388 Colleges by Princeton Review. The Psychology Department at Purchase is nationally ranked by the US News as a top undergraduate psychology program. Our department values inclusive research and teaching, as demonstrated through our commitment to student-faculty mentorship in our research-focused curriculum. In this open-area search, we welcome candidates who will be able to join the teaching rotation for some required courses (e.g., Introduction to Psychology, Research Methods, and Behavioral Statistics) and teach upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of specialization. The faculty teaching load is typically 6 courses per year (one course of which may be the supervision of six senior project students each year). Faculty are also expected to maintain active research programs and make meaningful contributions to campus service. Qualifications The successful candidate will be prepared to maintain an active research lab while providing research mentorship to undergraduate students from various backgrounds. Many undergraduate students at SUNY Purchase complete year-long senior projects, most involving empirical research (subject to IRB approval), under the supervision of a faculty sponsor. It is critically important that the candidate have the potential for, or presence of, an active publishing record and a passion for mentoring and advising undergraduate students from cross-sectional communities through the research process. The department is seeking applications from candidates who can demonstrate experience with diverse, multicultural populations through their own background, research training, or past teaching experiences. Candidates should highlight this in their application materials. A doctoral degree in Psychology or a related field by August 2027 is required. Candidates are required to complete an online application via the College’s job vacancy website. Applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, statements of Research Interests and Teaching Philosophy and a diversity statement (merged together and submitted as “other document 1”), as well as 2 representative publications (submitted as “other documents” 2 and 3). In addition, applicants are required to provide a list of contact information for three (3) references who can be contacted for a recommendation. Letters of reference will be requested for candidates identified to be interviewed. Letters of reference should NOT be sent or uploaded with your application materials. Phone calls, hard copy, or e-mail submissions of application materials will NOT be accepted. Special Note About Purchase College, SUNY A top 10 public school, according to U.S. News & World Report, Purchase College, part of the State University of New York ( SUNY ) system, is a dynamic campus that combines conservatory training in the visual and performing arts with programs in the liberal arts and sciences, in order to inspire an appreciation for both intellectual and artistic talents in all students. Purchase College, SUNY is a community of students, faculty, and friends where open-minded engagement with the creative process leads to a lifetime of intellectual growth and professional opportunity. For more information about the college, visit Purchase College. Benefits – • Health, dental, and vision benefits are available to eligible employees after a 28-day waiting period. More information regarding other benefits such as generous paid time off, tuition assistance, and retirement systems can be found on SUNY’s Benefit Summaries website . • Purchase College is a qualifying government employer allowing eligible employees to participate in the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. • Access to the NAEYC -accredited, on-campus child care at The Children’s Center. • Discounted access to the world-class Performing Arts Center, free admission to the Neuberger Museum of Art, and free access to the athletic facilities. • Other benefits include business-casual dress. For detailed information on some of the College’s employee benefits, visit the College’s Human Resources/Benefits website . Nondiscrimination Policy – Purchase College is committed to fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students, as well as ensuring equal educational opportunity, employment, and access to service, programs, and activities, without regard to an individual’s race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, or criminal conviction. Employees, students, applicants, or other members of the Purchase community (including vendors, visitors, and guests) may not be subjected to harassment that is prohibited by law or treated adversely or retaliated against based upon a protected characteristic. To view the entire policy, please visit the following website: Purchase College Human Resources Policies and Procedures website. Women, minorities, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Purchase College is an AA/ EEO employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three years; and the availability regarding the University’s current campus security policies. Purchase College’s Annual Security Report is available at Purchase College NYS University Police Website. Date to be Filled 09/01/2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 Optional Documents SUNY Purchase 735 Anderson Hill Road, Purchase, NY 10577 © SUNY Purchase To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.purchase.edu/postings/1775": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Painting and Drawing",
      "description": "Purchase College Portal | Assistant Professor of Painting and Drawing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Painting and Drawing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F068P Job Title Assistant Professor of Painting and Drawing Application Deadline 01/20/2027 Department School Of Art And Design FT - PT Full Time Part-time % Minimum Salary 65000.00 Maximum Salary 65000.00 Description The Painting and Drawing Department, School of Art+Design at SUNY Purchase, State University of New York, seeks applicants for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position. Teaching responsibilities include foundational, introductory, intermediate, and advanced studio and seminar courses. The new faculty member will teach in the BFA undergraduate program, and also mentor MFA students. Our ideal candidate will demonstrate a deep understanding and commitment to painting and pedagogy, and of broad approaches to art practice. Engagement with figurative or narrative approaches to painting is considered a plus. Other responsibilities include participation on departmental and college committees, student advising, admissions and recruitment, final reviews, curriculum building and other kinds of support as needed to maintain the programmatic offerings of the Painting+Drawing Department. Ability to lead and attend to administrative tasks are essential. Each faculty will serve as Chair of Painting + Drawing on a rotating basis. Qualifications A terminal degree in visual arts, or equivalent commensurate experience, is required. In addition, at least three years of teaching experience at the college/university level is preferred. The candidate should have professional standing and potential within their field. Salary: $65,000 + $4,316 location pay Applications are due: January 20, 2027, 11:59pm Application should include: • Cover letter and CV • 15-20 images of professional work as an internet link • 15-20 images of student work at various levels and a brief description of those assignments as an internet link • Artist’s Statement • Teaching Philosophy that describes the candidate’s general approach to art pedagogy, ideally with a few examples that demonstrate the ideas described. Special Note About Purchase College, SUNY A top 10 public school, according to U.S. News & World Report, Purchase College, part of the State University of New York ( SUNY ) system, is a dynamic campus that combines conservatory training in the visual and performing arts with programs in the liberal arts and sciences, in order to inspire an appreciation for both intellectual and artistic talents in all students. Purchase College, SUNY is a community of students, faculty, and friends where open-minded engagement with the creative process leads to a lifetime of intellectual growth and professional opportunity. For more information about the college, visit Purchase College. Benefits - • Health, dental, and vision benefits are available to eligible employees after a 28-day waiting period. More information regarding other benefits such as generous paid time off, tuition assistance, and retirement systems can be found on SUNY’s Benefit Summaries website . • Purchase College is a qualifying government employer allowing eligible employees to participate in the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. • Access to the NAEYC -accredited, on-campus child care at The Children’s Center. • Discounted access to the world-class Performing Arts Center, free admission to the Neuberger Museum of Art, and free access to the athletic facilities. • Other benefits include business-casual dress. For detailed information on some of the College’s employee benefits, visit the College’s Human Resources/Benefits website. Position is subject to a New York State Department of Civil Service Agency Reduction Transfer List clearance in accordance with NYS laws, rules, and regulations. Nondiscrimination Policy – Purchase College is committed to fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students, as well as ensuring equal educational opportunity, employment, and access to service, programs, and activities, without regard to an individual’s race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, or criminal conviction. Employees, students, applicants, or other members of the Purchase community (including vendors, visitors, and guests) may not be subjected to harassment that is prohibited by law or treated adversely or retaliated against based upon a protected characteristic. To view the entire policy, please visit the following website: Purchase College Human Resources Policies and Procedures website. Women, minorities, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Purchase College is an AA/ EEO employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three years; and the availability regarding the University’s current campus security policies. Purchase College’s Annual Security Report is available at Purchase College NYS University Police Website. Date to be Filled 09/01/2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents List of References Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 SUNY Purchase 735 Anderson Hill Road, Purchase, NY 10577 © SUNY Purchase To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivit