      "title": "Assistant Professor of Graphic Design",
      "description": "Purchase College Portal | Assistant Professor of Graphic Design Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Graphic Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F067P Job Title Assistant Professor of Graphic Design Application Deadline 01/20/2027 Department School Of Art And Design FT - PT Full Time Part-time % Minimum Salary 65000.00 Maximum Salary 65000.00 Description The Graphic Design program at the School of Art+Design at SUNY Purchase invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Graphic Design. The faculty member will teach in the program’s core undergraduate studio sequence beginning in the 2027-28 academic year. We seek a designer and educator whose practice is rooted in perennial design concerns of typography and visual communication, but extends into contemporary explorations of time-based media, interaction, and cultural critique. An ideal candidate has a practice which evidences conceptual rigor and addresses contemporary technological and ideological concerns, while maintaining formal ingenuity. Qualifications Candidates should hold an MFA or equivalent terminal degree and maintain a substantive personal or professional practice. A sustained commitment to inclusive pedagogy, critical dialogue, and interdisciplinary is intrinsic to the role. Especially of interest is an expansive practice coupling experience with traditional design tools such as letterpress, and print production with contemporary methodologies for the screen such as motion or interaction. Responsibilities Teaching (in person) undergraduate studio courses and advise senior projects Teach and advise across all levels of the undergraduate program, including the Foundations Program. Contribute to the creative and intellectual life of Graphic Design and the institution at large. This includes reviews, gatherings, exhibitions, workshops, and lectures. Participate in departmental service and curricular development. Required Qualifications MFA , equivalent terminal degree in graphic design or a related ?eld, or signi?cant equivalent professional experience. A robust portfolio of professional or creative graphic design work. One to three years of professional design experience, which may include independent practice. Knowledge of industry-standard production methods, software, and technology for print and digital media. This includes but is not limited to Adobe Creative Suite, Figma, Cavalry, and risography. Commitment to teaching students from varied backgrounds and with di?erent levels of experience. Undergraduate teaching experience or demonstrated potential to teach at this level. Preferred Qualifications A commitment to diverse design histories, inclusive pedagogy, and critical engagement with contemporary visual culture. Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration within a public liberal arts college. Familiarity with contemporary technologies for interactivity, motion, and production. Experience with letterpress, printmaking, or other related “analog” production skills. About the Program The four-year Graphic Design department at SUNY Purchase o?ers a unique, forward-thinking curriculum that integrates the art and practice of both print and digital design. From letterpress and artist books to interactive installations and motion design, students engage with a wide range of media and methodologies. Grounded in design history and responsive to emerging technologies, the program prepares students to navigate—and shape—the rapidly evolving landscape of contemporary visual communication. Salary: $65,000 + $4,316 location pay Applications are due: January 20, 2027, 11:59pm Application should include: Cover letter describing your qualifications and teaching interests\\ Curriculum vitae Portfolio of design work ( PDF or website link) Statement of teaching philosophy Names and contact information for three references Special Note About Purchase College, SUNY A top 10 public school, according to U.S. News & World Report, Purchase College, part of the State University of New York ( SUNY ) system, is a dynamic campus that combines conservatory training in the visual and performing arts with programs in the liberal arts and sciences, in order to inspire an appreciation for both intellectual and artistic talents in all students. Purchase College, SUNY is a community of students, faculty, and friends where open-minded engagement with the creative process leads to a lifetime of intellectual growth and professional opportunity. For more information about the college, visit Purchase College. Benefits - • Health, dental, and vision benefits are available to eligible employees after a 28-day waiting period. More information regarding other benefits such as generous paid time off, tuition assistance, and retirement systems can be found on SUNY’s Benefit Summaries website . • Purchase College is a qualifying government employer allowing eligible employees to participate in the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. • Access to the NAEYC -accredited, on-campus child care at The Children’s Center. • Discounted access to the world-class Performing Arts Center, free admission to the Neuberger Museum of Art, and free access to the athletic facilities. • Other benefits include business-casual dress. For detailed information on some of the College’s employee benefits, visit the College’s Human Resources/Benefits website. Position is subject to a New York State Department of Civil Service Agency Reduction Transfer List clearance in accordance with NYS laws, rules, and regulations. Nondiscrimination Policy – Purchase College is committed to fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students, as well as ensuring equal educational opportunity, employment, and access to service, programs, and activities, without regard to an individual’s race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, or criminal conviction. Employees, students, applicants, or other members of the Purchase community (including vendors, visitors, and guests) may not be subjected to harassment that is prohibited by law or treated adversely or retaliated against based upon a protected characteristic. To view the entire policy, please visit the following website: Purchase College Human Resources Policies and Procedures website. Women, minorities, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Purchase College is an AA/ EEO employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three years; and the availability regarding the University’s current campus security policies. Purchase College’s Annual Security Report is available at Purchase College NYS University Police Website. Date to be Filled 09/01/2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio List of References Other Document 1 Optional Documents Other Document 2 SUNY Purchase 735 Anderson Hill Road, Purchase, NY 10577 © SUNY Purchase To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
